  "lineage": "French interwar composer-collective (Georges Auric, Louis Durey, Arthur Honegger, Darius Milhaud, Francis Poulenc, Germaine Tailleferre) named in 1920 by critic Henri Collet by analogy with the Russian Mighty Five. Aesthetic of Cocteau-inspired anti-Romantic clarity, accessible-melodic neoclassicism, jazz-and-popular-music integration, and Parisian cafe-and-music-hall aesthetic. Erik Satie served as elder-mentor figure. The 1921 Les Mariés de la tour Eiffel ballet (collective composition) is the canonical group-document.",
